# Add patterns of files dvc should ignore, which could improve
# the performance. Learn more at
# https://dvc.org/doc/user-guide/dvcignore

# Python bytecode caches.
#
# Datasets that embed this workflow as a submodule typically declare
# `modules/snp_demux/workflow` as a DVC dependency. If a workflow script ever
# imports a sibling module, Python writes .pyc files into
# workflow/scripts/__pycache__/, and bytecode is not reproducible — its size and
# contents depend on the interpreter version and on source mtimes — so the
# dependency can never hash equal twice. The stage then reports "changed deps"
# on every `dvc repro`, which for an expensive stage means either re-running it
# or freezing it to work around the drift.
#
# Pre-emptive here: workflow/scripts/*.py are currently run as scripts rather
# than imported, so no bytecode is written yet. The sibling modules
# chromium-preprocessing and mkobj have already hit this.
#
# Ignoring these loses nothing: .pyc files are derived from .py files that are
# themselves tracked.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
